# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in what you need. Both settings are
# optional. The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix is required for Expo to expose a value to
# the app, and Metro must be restarted (npx expo start -c) after a change.

# PocketBase server to start in on a fresh install. Accounts and the library
# then live on the server and follow you across devices. Leave it empty to
# start on the device. Either way the Storage setting in the app (Me tab,
# Settings, Advanced, or "Advanced" on the Login screen) can switch later, and
# a saved choice wins over this value. Setup steps are in pocketbase/README.md.
EXPO_PUBLIC_POCKETBASE_URL=

# Lookup keys for the "Fill from the web" button in the add form. All three
# are optional and free. Without any of them the button still works for
# series (TVmaze) and books (Open Library, Google Books); films need TMDB or
# OMDb.

# TMDB, films and series, and the most up to date. Either the "API key" or the
# "API Read Access Token" from https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api works.
EXPO_PUBLIC_TMDB_API_KEY=

# OMDb, films and series. Free key (1,000 requests/day) at:
#   https://www.omdbapi.com/apikey.aspx
EXPO_PUBLIC_OMDB_API_KEY=

# Google Books works without a key. A key from the Google Cloud console only
# raises the daily quota, which is otherwise shared.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=
